From 889280a2dddb800bb82a2a8cff27b15136016bdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:07:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] provider: a Command Code Credits window renews at the plan's
 period's end
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

#2451 made a Command Code card show the month's credits as a Credits
meter beside the 5-hour and weekly ones. Those two each say when they
start again; the Credits meter said nothing, though the end of the
plan's period — when the month's credits come back — is in the same
billing/subscriptions reply the plan is read from. On the card, where
every other window had a reset line, the month's alone had none.

cmdQuotaOf takes the period's end and puts it on the Credits window.
The signed-in subscription's card passes the one its own
billing/subscriptions reply carries; a plan key's card gets it from
cmdKeyPlanID beside the plan id, and the pair read before is kept while
the endpoint can't be read, as the id was. No period end, no reset — a
card reads as before.

Run:
- New TestCommandCodeCreditsWindowRenewsAtPeriodEnd, on both cards.
  On the unfixed tree it went red: "the key card's credits have no
  reset", "the subscription card's credits have no reset". With the
  change, green.
- TestCommandCodeKeyCardHasCredits, TestKeyQuotasKeepLast,
  TestCommandCodeQuotaShowsWindows (its two cmdQuotaOf calls pass nil)
  and the rest of the Command Code tests stay green.
- go test -tags nogui -p 2 ./internal/provider/ ./internal/usage/
  ./internal/catalog/, every package ok.
- gofmt; go vet -tags nogui for darwin, linux and windows.
- Not tried against Command Code's real API: there is no plan key here.

